  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Danish contribution to the PPIMA project phase IV</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of the PPIMA project phase IV, the Danish contribution will seek to introduce and scale-up NPA&#x2019;s work around citizens&#x2019; environment protection and climate change action awareness, including strengthening citizens, CSOs and local leaders&#x2019; policy literacy on human rights and environment &amp; climate change to accelerate commitments to adopting environment-friendly practices and establishing the framework for wider environmental and related social justice. This includes laying the foundation for citizen-led independent monitoring and reporting on duty bearers&#x2019; compliance with the environmental and social management safeguards in planning implementing public and community-led infrastructure projects. 

The anticipated outcomes are:
 - Outcome 1: Civil Society partners are more effective in their work to influence and mobilize.
 - Outcome 2: Citizens acted and participated in decision-making for their rights.
 - Outcome 3: Local and national government have formulated policies and plans that reflect the concerns raised by citizens and gender equality considerations.</narrative>
  </description>
